# Uptime Kuma safety

## Gate

Load on every authorized Uptime Kuma turn (inventory or mutate). Skip when
the turn never touches Uptime Kuma.

## Read-only default

These are fine without an extra destructive verb when Uptime Kuma is
authorized:

- list monitors, heartbeats, status pages, tags
- list notification channels (names/types only)
- read one monitor's status

Do **not** delete, bulk-pause, or change notification credentials unless the
user gave an explicit verb **this turn** naming the object(s).

## Mutate gates (explicit verb required)

| Risk | Needs this turn |
| --- | --- |
| Create / update monitor or page | **create**/**update** + fields |
| Pause / resume | **pause**/**resume** + id(s) |
| Delete monitor / page / channel | **delete** + id |
| Bulk pause | **pause** + listed ids (not "all") |
| Notification credential change | **update** + channel id (no secret echo) |

Ambiguous "clean up old monitors" → ask for ids; do not mass-delete.

## Prefer pause

Prefer pause over delete when the user only wants quiet. Delete is
permanent for that monitor's history on many setups — say so.

## Refuse

- Pasting API keys or notification webhook secrets into chat
- Inventing monitor / tag / status-page ids
- Absorbing Prometheus/Grafana alerting fleets into this surface
- Bulk-acting without listed ids

## Receipt examples (safe)

Inventory turn: monitor `api-prod` id `12` type `http` status `up` — no
mutate.

Pause turn (authorized): paused monitor `12` — no webhook secrets.

